senses.gloss:
नरङ्ग नरङ्ग, अस्, m. pimples on the face
(= वरण्डक); (अम्), n. the penis; (wrong form
for नराङ्ग, see col. 1.)

नर्त नर्त, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. rt. नृत्, the initial
न् of which is not liable to become ण्), dancing;
(अस्), m. dancing, dance.

नर्दन, अस्, m. ‘one who roars,’ N. of a Nāga-
rāja; (अम्), n. sounding, roaring, making a noise;
celebrating, praising aloud.

नर्दटक नर्दटक, अम्, n. a kind of metre
consisting of four lines of seventeen syllables each;
(wrongly written नर्धटक; cf. नर्कुटक.)

नारीक at the end of an adj. comp. = नारी;
(अम्), n. (in the Sāṅkhya phil.) one of the nine
kinds of Tuṣṭi.
